course: dictionary
lesson: 14840
title: Raffle: a word about tickets and chance
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A raffle is a way to raise money. People buy numbered tickets, then some tickets are picked out to win prizes. Context helps here: «The school held a raffle at the summer fair to raise money for new books.» Tickets, prizes and money are the clues.
explain: Raffle can also be a verb, a doing word. «The club will raffle a cake at the fête.» Here raffle means to offer something as a prize in a raffle. Check by swapping in your meaning: "The club will offer a cake as a raffle prize" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Raffle is also a chance word. «Mia bought five tickets, so she had five chances to win.» If 100 tickets are sold, five tickets give her a 5 in 100 chance of winning. Words and maths meet here.
fact: A raffle is a way of raising money with numbered tickets.
fact: The tickets that are picked out win the prizes.
fact: «Raffle» can be a noun (a raffle) or a verb (to raffle something).
fact: Schools, clubs and churches often hold raffles at fairs and fêtes to raise money for charity.
fact: If 100 tickets are sold and you buy 5, your chance of winning the one prize is 5 in 100.
exercise: «The school held a raffle to raise money for new books.» What is a raffle? | A type of cake sold at fairs | *A way of raising money with numbered tickets and prizes | A race to see who runs fastest | A list of books in the library
exercise: «The club will raffle a cake at the fête.» What does raffle mean here? | *To offer a cake as a prize in a raffle | To lose a cake on purpose | To bake a cake for a party | To eat the cake quickly
exercise: «Ten tickets are sold and Sam buys two.» What is Sam's chance of winning the one prize? | 2 in 100 | 1 in 10 is his chance, not 2 in 10 | *2 in 10 | 10 in 2
test: In «Dad bought a raffle ticket at the fair», what kind of ticket is it? | A train ticket | *A ticket for a raffle | A cinema ticket | A bus ticket
test: «Twenty tickets are sold and Ava buys four.» What is her chance of winning the one prize? | 24 in 20 | *4 in 20 | 20 in 4 | 4 in 2
exam: Which sentence uses raffle as a verb? | «The raffle prize was a teddy bear.» | *«The club will raffle a bike to help the school.» | «The fair had a raffle stall.» | «Ben bought a raffle ticket.»
